@*
    The root document. Static-rendered on purpose: it emits <html>, which cannot be part of
    an interactive component tree. Interactivity starts one level down, at <Routes/>.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>Hephaisto</title>
    @* Local stylesheets only. This pod may run in a cluster with no egress, and a console
       whose CSS silently fails to load is unreadable at exactly the moment it is needed.

       Two files, one origin. tokens.css is the canonical token set and MUST come first: it
       defines the custom properties app.css then reads. Both are served from this pod's own
       wwwroot and fingerprinted by MapStaticAssets, so this is not a second network dependency
       - which is the thing the no-CDN rule is actually about. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["tokens.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    @* Was href="data:," - the trick that suppresses the 404 by shipping no icon at all. There
       is an icon now. SVG only and no .ico fallback: this console is reached by whoever is on
       call, on a current browser, and every one of them has supported SVG favicons for years. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="@Assets["favicon.svg"]" type="image/svg+xml" />

    @* theme-color paints the browser chrome to match the console rather than leaving a white
       bar above a dark page. Two values, because light mode stopped being a courtesy in
       v0.4.0. *@
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#212123" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f8f7f8" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />

    @* Stamps a remembered theme onto <html> BEFORE the first paint.

       Inline and synchronous, which is the whole point: app.js is loaded at the end of <body>,
       so a reader who chose light would get a full paint of the dark theme and then a flip.
       That flash is worse than not offering the choice.

       Guarded because localStorage THROWS outright in some privacy modes rather than returning
       null, and a convenience must never be able to take the console down. No value, or a
       value this does not recognise, means "system" - the OS decides through the media query,
       which is what every release before v0.5.0 did. *@
    <script>
        (function () {
            try {
                var t = window.localStorage.getItem('hephaisto.theme');
                if (t === 'light' || t === 'dark') {
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
                }
            } catch (e) {
                /* Private window, disabled storage. Fall through to the OS. */
            }
        })();
    </script>
    <meta name="description" content="Hephaisto investigates Kubernetes incidents, acts only where it is allowed to, and escalates to a human when it cannot prove a fix." />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    @*
        The reconnect overlay. Blazor drives this purely by id and by the classes it puts on
        the container - if the element is absent, as it was here, a dropped circuit produces
        NO indication of any kind: the page keeps rendering the last state it received, the
        durations stop ticking, and a stale incident list is indistinguishable from a quiet
        cluster. That is the same failure the AgentWatchdog exists to prevent, one layer up,
        and it is worse here because a human is looking straight at it and being reassured.

        The circuit drops on every pod restart, so this is the ordinary case, not the
        exotic one.
    *@
    <div id="components-reconnect-modal" class="hp-reconnect">
        <div class="hp-reconnect-box">
            <p class="hp-reconnect-title">Connection to the agent lost</p>

            <p class="hp-reconnect-retrying">
                Reconnecting, attempt <span id="components-reconnect-current-attempt"></span>
                of <span id="components-reconnect-max-retries"></span>.
            </p>

            <p class="hp-reconnect-failed">
                Could not reconnect.
                <button type="button" onclick="location.reload()">Reload the page</button>
            </p>

            <p class="hp-reconnect-note">
                This page is frozen. Nothing on it has updated since the connection dropped,
                and it may be badly out of date.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["app.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
